---
config:
  layout: elk
  elk:
    nodePlacementStrategy: BRANDES_KOEPF
---
flowchart TB
    %% Line language, applied consistently:
    %%   -->    code moves, in the direction it moves
    %%   -.->   an answer comes back — a query, nothing shipped
    %% Bold is an action somebody takes; normal weight is something that
    %% happens on its own or a question being asked. Bold comes from
    %% mermaid markdown strings (backtick-quoted labels) rather than <b>,
    %% which leaks literally while htmlLabels is false.
    %% .
    %% Every arrow is numbered, in the order events happen, so the whole
    %% sequence can be followed by reading the numbers. The numbers ARE the
    %% runbook's section numbers in docs/3.3 part 1 — arrow 1.5 is step 1.5 —
    %% so the diagram and the text can be read together. A third level breaks
    %% one step into its ordered parts: 1.1.1-1.1.2 are things you do,
    %% 1.6.1-1.6.5 are what one command does on your behalf.
    %% .
    %% This was 1.a, 2.b, 6.e until 2026-08-21, a second numbering scheme
    %% sitting beside the section numbers and agreeing with neither.
    %% .
    %%   {  }   a decision on an action arrow — the action stops here and
    %%          is tested before it continues. Checks feed into it.
    %% .
    %% .
    %% Preview DOES feed the gate, and this comment said the opposite until
    %% 2026-09-09. A preview gate exists in deploy.sh, counted by
    %% `note_gate preview`, and refuses when preview is running a different
    %% commit. deploy.sh carried the identical stale paragraph directly above
    %% its own gate and was corrected in bb0f376; the diagram was not.
    %% .
    %% What survives of the old argument is the honest limit rather than the
    %% conclusion: the gate proves this commit was *deployed* to preview, and
    %% cannot prove anybody looked at it and was happy. Whether a person formed
    %% a judgement is not observable from here. So it is a prompt, and the only
    %% one available for the question.
    %% .
    %% The gate is a decision on the *action*, not a property of production:
    %% it happens inside deploy.sh, before anything ships, and the two
    %% checks are inputs to it. Drawing it as arrows into Production implied
    %% a relationship between Actions and Production that does not exist.
    %% .
    %% No linkStyle anywhere: the shapes carry the meaning. Edge indices
    %% silently pointed at the wrong arrows four times when they did.
    %% .
    %% Steps 3, 6 and 7.a start at local git rather than Dev on purpose, and
    %% this is literally true of the scripts: both check the commit out into
    %% a throwaway git worktree and build that, so the working tree cannot
    %% reach either environment. Do not "correct" these to start at DEV.
    DEV["Dev<br/>working tree<br/>:3000 server · :8080 web"]
    STG["Preview<br/>:8081 · docker"]
    REH["Rehearsal<br/>&lt;ip&gt;.sslip.io · docker"]
    PROD["Production<br/>tileliteelite.com"]
    LG["local git<br/>commit history"]
    subgraph GH["GitHub"]
        REPO["repo · main"]
        ACT["Actions"]
    end


    DEV ~~~ STG
    STG ~~~ REH
    REH ~~~ GATE
    %% Without this, ELK floats Production up beside the others and "ships
    %% the image" points upward. Pinning it last puts the environments in
    %% descending order and the deploy flow downward through the gate.
    REH ~~~ PROD

    DEV -->|"`1.1.1 · **$ cargo build**
**$ services.sh restart**
**$ cargo test**`"| DEV
    DEV -->|"`1.1.2 · **$ git add**
**$ git commit**`"| LG
    LG -->|"`1.2.1 · **$ git push**`"| REPO
    REPO -->|"1.2.2 · CI runs (automatic)"| ACT
    ACT -.->|"`1.2.3 · **$ ci-status.sh --wait**`"| LG
    PROD -.->|"`1.3.1 · **$ deploy-preview.sh at prod**`"| STG
    LG -->|"`1.3.2 · **$ deploy-preview.sh**`"| STG
    STG -.->|"`1.3.3 · **$ curl /health**`"| STG
    STG -.->|"`1.4 · **user test**`"| STG
    LG -->|"`1.5 · **$ deploy-rehearsal.sh**`"| REH
    LG -->|"`1.6.1 · **$ deploy.sh**`"| GATE{"gate"}
    GATE -->|"1.6.4 · ships the image"| PROD
    ACT -.->|"1.6.2 · CI green for this commit?"| GATE
    STG -.->|"1.6.2a · preview on this commit?"| GATE
    REH -.->|"1.6.3 · rehearsal on this commit?"| GATE
    LG -->|"1.6.5 · tag + version bump"| REPO
    PROD -.->|"`1.7 · **$ deploy-preview.sh verify**`"| STG

    classDef gate fill:#fbe9dc,stroke:#b06a2c,color:#7a4318
    classDef env fill:#e4eff8,stroke:#39698c,color:#12303f
    classDef repo fill:#f7efe0,stroke:#96763f,color:#3a2c12
    class DEV,STG,REH,PROD env
    class LG,REPO,ACT repo
    class GATE gate
    style GH fill:#fdf9f1,stroke:#96763f,color:#3a2c12
